4
00:00:14,471 --> 00:00:15,799
Experimental timing files.

5
00:00:15,799 --> 00:00:24,656
An F S L three-column timing file has one event per row: onset in seconds, duration in seconds, and amplitude.

6
00:00:24,656 --> 00:00:27,755
Each condition normally has its own file.

7
00:00:27,755 --> 00:00:32,183
Timing is relative to the start of the modeled run.

8
00:00:32,183 --> 00:00:37,940
Units, missing events, and condition labels must be checked against the BIDS events.

9
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:38,826
tsv file.

10
00:00:38,826 --> 00:00:43,254
A syntactically valid file can still encode the wrong experiment.

11
00:00:44,104 --> 00:00:47,456
Now connect the idea to an observable check.

12
00:00:47,456 --> 00:00:49,551
First, open a matching events.

13
00:00:49,551 --> 00:00:50,389
tsv file.

14
00:00:50,389 --> 00:00:52,065
